{"title":"imagining labyrinth library","link":"https://keningzhu.com/journal/imagining-labyrinth-library","date":1756366140000,"content":"<figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/labyrinth\">\n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/26260b47-e632-4efb-a718-6a0654ad2e0e/labyrinthlibrarykeningzhu-26August2025-ezgif.com-video-to-gif-converter.gif?format=1000w\" width=\"800\" height=\"470\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/26260b47-e632-4efb-a718-6a0654ad2e0e/labyrinthlibrarykeningzhu-26August2025-ezgif.com-video-to-gif-converter.gif?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/26260b47-e632-4efb-a718-6a0654ad2e0e/labyrinthlibrarykeningzhu-26August2025-ezgif.com-video-to-gif-converter.gif?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/26260b47-e632-4efb-a718-6a0654ad2e0e/labyrinthlibrarykeningzhu-26August2025-ezgif.com-video-to-gif-converter.gif?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/26260b47-e632-4efb-a718-6a0654ad2e0e/labyrinthlibrarykeningzhu-26August2025-ezgif.com-video-to-gif-converter.gif?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/26260b47-e632-4efb-a718-6a0654ad2e0e/labyrinthlibrarykeningzhu-26August2025-ezgif.com-video-to-gif-converter.gif?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/26260b47-e632-4efb-a718-6a0654ad2e0e/labyrinthlibrarykeningzhu-26August2025-ezgif.com-video-to-gif-converter.gif?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/26260b47-e632-4efb-a718-6a0654ad2e0e/labyrinthlibrarykeningzhu-26August2025-ezgif.com-video-to-gif-converter.gif?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          </a>\n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <p><strong>visit </strong><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/labyrinth\"><strong>labyrinth library</strong></a><strong><br /></strong><em>season 1 begins end of september</em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p>for a few years now, I’ve been dreaming of creating an ongoing community offering. I’ve hesitated and grappled with how I might make the “membership model” feel exciting and aligned for me. I finally felt ready for something regular and grounding. I wanted something more ongoing/communal than a course. <em>and</em>, I wanted an offering vessel that I could continue to pour my creative energy into — which would only become richer, denser, and more layered, over time.</p><p></p><h1>library, garden, labyrinth  </h1><p>I came up with <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/labyrinth\">labyrinth library</a> — as an alchemical concoction between a <strong>library </strong>and a <strong>garden</strong>. a library is a place you go to dream and study; to immerse in ideas, to follow threads of possibilities, worlds, fantasies. </p><p>a garden is a place you go to be surrounded by beauty, nature, the seasons, and to witness the cycles of life and death. both are spaces that hold you, nourish you, offer you refuge, provide infinite paths to wander through. both are spaces that are very much alive. </p><p>the word “labyrinth” has been on my mind since last year, when I wrote this piece, “<a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/build-a-labyrinth-not-a-funnel\" target=\"_blank\">build a labyrinth, not a marketing funnel</a>.” a labyrinth, unlike a maze, is not for getting lost — but for being in the process of walking the path, towards the center. </p><p>we are each alone in our own labyrinths — in our creative work, our businesses, and in life itself. it felt like the right name for an ongoing offering that will stay very close to my heart; itself at the center of my ecosystem. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e1fb8a12-8214-4c92-a22a-c86e07b62021/notebook1.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e1fb8a12-8214-4c92-a22a-c86e07b62021/notebook1.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e1fb8a12-8214-4c92-a22a-c86e07b62021/notebook1.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e1fb8a12-8214-4c92-a22a-c86e07b62021/notebook1.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e1fb8a12-8214-4c92-a22a-c86e07b62021/notebook1.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e1fb8a12-8214-4c92-a22a-c86e07b62021/notebook1.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e1fb8a12-8214-4c92-a22a-c86e07b62021/notebook1.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/e1fb8a12-8214-4c92-a22a-c86e07b62021/notebook1.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  <p>after teaching <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/sharing-space-camp\">sharing space camp</a> this july/august, I decided that I was ready to open the first season of labyrinth this fall. </p><p>I started by opening a sketchbook, and drawing visuals that called to me — <em>a moth, an eye, a rose, a keyhole, a ladder, a potion, a door.</em> I don’t know where these images came from, other than that they felt like artifacts and symbols of initiation into a mystery. they came to me, and I drew them.  <br /></p><h1>at the heart of labyrinth </h1><p>later that day, while walking along a noisy street to the tax office to do bureaucractic nonsense, I had an ephiphany. I knew that labyrinth was at the heart of my ecosystem. I realized, then, what was at the heart of labyrinth. it was a simple phrase. </p><p>“<strong><em>being with the unknown</em></strong>” </p><p>it sounds so obvious, and even borderline a spiritual platitude. but the work of being with the unknown <em>is</em> what has been the life source of ALL of my work. it is how I do my <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/lonely-work-is-swimming-in-the-ocean-alone\" target=\"_blank\">lonely work</a>, how I confront <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/creative-courage-in-the-digital-void\" target=\"_blank\">the void</a>, imagine new paths, make art, exist on the internet, build businesses, and generally, live my life. </p><p>I would not be <em>me</em> — without my devotion to the unknown. and no matter how “stable” my life feels, my reverence for the unknown <em>(and therefore chaotic, terrifying, sublime, primordial)</em> forces is what keeps my work and life feeling electric, mysterious, and alive. </p><p>the unknown is at the heart of everything. it is what I want to spend all year, all four seasons thinking about, because making work about mystery, about unpredictability, about what <em>we don’t know</em> — is the only possible way I won’t get bored. this is the way for me to continually be inspired.  </p><p>in other words, labyrinth is the path of <strong>mystery studies.</strong> I am simultaneously a teacher, a student, a guide, a wanderer. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/75c27ee6-7d1f-4292-9d9e-34eab322e836/notebook2.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/75c27ee6-7d1f-4292-9d9e-34eab322e836/notebook2.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/75c27ee6-7d1f-4292-9d9e-34eab322e836/notebook2.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/75c27ee6-7d1f-4292-9d9e-34eab322e836/notebook2.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/75c27ee6-7d1f-4292-9d9e-34eab322e836/notebook2.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/75c27ee6-7d1f-4292-9d9e-34eab322e836/notebook2.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/75c27ee6-7d1f-4292-9d9e-34eab322e836/notebook2.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/75c27ee6-7d1f-4292-9d9e-34eab322e836/notebook2.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  <p>once I found that heart of the offering, the rest of it felt… easy. I knew that there were structural things I wanted to create inside the container of labyrinth — <em>monthly workshops, illustrated zines, artifacts, discussion sessions, 10 day challenges, community containers,</em> <em>tarot diaries, experimental things…</em> </p><p>but more than that, I wanted labyrinth to be my personal creative teaching playground; a space where I felt safe and energetically nourished to give an outpouring of raw ideas, frameworks, processes, possibilities. it is like a veiled version of my website, which itself is the “public gardens” of my work. labyrinth is a gated, mysterious place at its very heart center. <br /><br /></p><h1>making version 0.1 of the invitations page</h1><p>I usually approach new offerings by imagining the visuals first. from my notebook, I selected 4 ideas <em>(moth, eye, key, rose)</em> and did a 3 minute sketch of each, and laid it out on a new page. this is what I had outlined in 50 minutes, set with placeholder text:  </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/ad783c65-2bf9-4f8b-b1d8-0eaded76489f/labyrinth_00_1.png?format=1000w\" width=\"3446\" height=\"1930\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/ad783c65-2bf9-4f8b-b1d8-0eaded76489f/labyrinth_00_1.png?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/ad783c65-2bf9-4f8b-b1d8-0eaded76489f/labyrinth_00_1.png?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/ad783c65-2bf9-4f8b-b1d8-0eaded76489f/labyrinth_00_1.png?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/ad783c65-2bf9-4f8b-b1d8-0eaded76489f/labyrinth_00_1.png?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/ad783c65-2bf9-4f8b-b1d8-0eaded76489f/labyrinth_00_1.png?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/ad783c65-2bf9-4f8b-b1d8-0eaded76489f/labyrinth_00_1.png?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/ad783c65-2bf9-4f8b-b1d8-0eaded76489f/labyrinth_00_1.png?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  <p>I had previously came up with the dark forest green “labyrinth library” image a few months ago, when I made <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/opening-a-soon-page\" target=\"_blank\">the soon page</a>. after dropping in these 4 sketches, I had a minimalist, skeletal structure that conveyed the <em>essence</em> of labyrinth, and got me feeling excited about it. this is the key — making <em>myself</em> excited to keep working on it. </p><p>then, over the next few days, I let momentum carry me. I wrote about the offering. I redrew the visuals, with a detached pleasure. I swapped out the eye for a door. I put a “coming soon” button. I let my mind simmer on what it wanted to create for labyrinth, next — I think an illustrated zine, or an animation. I mapped out a timeline of how I’d share labyrinth, and when I’d open the door. and, just like that, version 0.1 of my <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/labyrinth\">labyrinth invitations page</a> was done. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n     